In article <2406@sunset.MATH.UCLA.EDU>, jborzell@oak.math.ucla.edu (joseph borzellino) writes:
> I am playing nethack 3.0 pl7, and am getting a memory fault when I kick
>   walls.  I've been reading this newsgroup consistently and no one else
>   seems to have the same problem.   Any help would be appreciated.
> 
This bug will be fixed in patch 8. It happens when you kick an object, and
that object is later used up, and you then kick a wall or piece of furniture.
The work-around is to always make sure that the last object you kicked is
still around (the dog hasn't eaten it, or whatever) before kicking a wall.
